### Key design decisions

| Concern | Resolution |
|---|---|
| Existing dir (idempotent) | `mkdir` returns EEXIST → `stat` confirms `S_ISDIR` → success, **no chmod** |
| Existing non-dir | EEXIST → `stat` shows not a dir → errno set to `ENOTDIR`, reported via `strerror` |
| Symlink resolving to dir | `stat()` follows the link, `S_ISDIR` true → accepted |
| Owner wx on intermediates | Only applied to **newly created** intermediates (`mkdir` returned 0); existing ones are left untouched |
| Trailing / repeated slashes | A `/` is treated as an intermediate boundary only if a non-slash byte follows it; otherwise it's part of the final path |
| Absolute paths | Leading `/` and the root prefix `/` are skipped; the kernel resolves the rest |
| Options after operands | Two-pass design: first pass parses all tokens (options + operands interleaved), second pass performs mutations |
| `malloc` failure | Sets `errno = ENOMEM`, returns error (no undefined behaviour) |

